invariant: INV-64
file: srv.c
catches: cnsa2_server_test
reason: the profile's server takes a ch_cfg.cpu that holds CH_CPU_PROBED
  alone, so a session without the caller's AES statement would run
  AES-256-GCM, the profile's one suite, and its tickets, on instructions
  nobody stated the timing of. test_identity_and_cpu requires
  srv_config_ok and ch_srv_check to refuse that value.

--- old
    return (cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0;
--- new
    return (cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_PROBED) != 0;
